    categories: ["geopolitica"],
    title: "Spanish authorities under pressure after record number of migrants reach Canaries",
    summary: "With a general election less than a week away, pressure is mounting on Spanish authorities over the growing number of migrant arrivals. More than 350 people in about six small boats reached the Canary Island's El Hierro on Sunday. That brings the total number of migrants being housed on the island",
    preview: "With a general election less than a week away, pressure is mounting on Spanish authorities over the growing number of migrant arrivals. More than 350 people in about six small boats reached the Canary Island's El Hierro on Sunday. That brings the total number of migrants being housed on the island",
    body: "Spain\n\nWith a general election less than a week away, pressure is mounting on Spanish authorities over the growing number of migrant arrivals.\n\nMore than 350 people in about six small boats reached the Canary Island's El Hierro on Sunday, bringing the total number of migrants being housed on the island to around 900.\n\nHome to just 12,000 people, reception capacity on El Hierro is under tremendous pressure.\n\nMore than 2,500 migrants reached the Canaries over the weekend, the highest number ever recorded for a single day.\n\nOverall, November has seen more than 10,000 migrants reach the Canary Islands - another record for the Spanish archipelago.\n\nSpanish authorities have announced 5 million euros in emergency aid. That's on top of more than 15 million euros previously announced for reception facilities and transfers.\n\nThe new wave of arrivals has pushed migration and border control to the top of the agenda for many voters in Sunday's election. Polls show the right-wing Popular Party leading the pack but falling short of a majority.\n\nIncumbent prime minister Pedro Sanchez has been under fire over the mass influx of migrants into the North African enclave of Ceuta in July.",
