    title: "Prabowo names two candidates to replace Gibran as Indonesia’s vice president",
    summary: "Indonesia's parliament is scheduled to convene a plenary session on Dec 11 to select the new vice president after vetting the two candidates.",
    preview: "Indonesia's parliament is scheduled to convene a plenary session on Dec 11 to select the new vice president after vetting the two candidates. JAKARTA: Indonesia’s Minister of Human Development and Culture Sugiono and Minister of Agriculture Andi Amran Sulaiman have been named as candidates to become vice president to replace Gibran Rakabuming Raka who resigned earlier this month.",
    body: "Indonesia's parliament is scheduled to convene a plenary session on Dec 11 to select the new vice president after vetting the two candidates.\n\nJAKARTA: Indonesia’s Minister of Human Development and Culture Sugiono and Minister of Agriculture Andi Amran Sulaiman have been named as candidates to become vice president to replace Gibran Rakabuming Raka who resigned earlier this month.\n\nIndonesia's President Prabowo Subianto submitted the names to the People’s Consultative Assembly (MPR) on Monday (Nov 23) evening following a meeting earlier in the day, local media reported.\n\nThe candidates were announced by MPR Chairman Ahmad Muzani, who read out a letter from the president at the parliament complex.\n\n\"Herewith, I propose the vice presidential candidates for the Republic of Indonesia, namely Andi Amran Sulaiman and Sugiono,” said Muzani.\n\nLawmakers will convene on December 11 to choose between Andi and former foreign minister Sugiono, who is the ruling party’s secretary-general.\n\n\"I believe that both of them will do their best for the nation, the state, and the people of Indonesia,\" Prabowo told reporters.\n\nSugiono, who like many Indonesians uses only one name, is sometimes referred to as the president's \"ideological child\" due to their close working relationship.\n\nA vice president from Prabowo's party could help \"secure the popularity\" of the president ahead of a potential re-election bid in 2029, Centre for Strategic and International Studies researcher Dominique Nicky Fachrizal told AFP before the nomination.\n\nThe 47-year-old Sugiono, who had a short stint in the army's special forces unit before retiring in 2004, was made coordinating minister for human development and cultural affairs in a cabinet reshuffle last month.\n\nAndi, 58, was a businessman before serving as the agriculture minister under Widodo, also known as Jokowi, between 2014 and 2019.\n\nHe returned to the post following a corruption scandal involving his successor, and was re-appointed when Prabowo came to power in 2024.\n\nGibran, the eldest son of Prabowo’s predecessor Joko Widodo, resigned on Nov 12 following weeks of political pressure amid legal cases over the validity of his qualifications in running for the post.\n\nIndonesia’s Supreme Court had annulled the 39-year-old’s overseas high school education equivalency certificate on Oct 30.\n\nGibran's resignation earlier this month is widely seen as a sign of a fraying political partnership between Prabowo and the popular two-term former president Widodo, who is better known as Jokowi, raising the possibility of a significant shift in politics.",
